\begin{didyouknow}{Determinants Before Matrices}
Determinants are older than matrices. Seki Takakazu described them in Japan in 1683, and Gottfried Leibniz independently used them in 1693 to solve systems of linear equations. The word \emph{determinant} in its modern sense comes from Augustin-Louis Cauchy in 1812. Matrices as objects in their own right arrived only in the 1850s, more than 150 years after the determinant.
\end{didyouknow}
% DYK-END

