\begin{didyouknow}{A Word From Sylvester}
James Joseph Sylvester coined the word \emph{matrix} in 1850, from the Latin for womb, because he saw a rectangular array as the source from which determinants are born. His friend Arthur Cayley published the first systematic algebra of matrices in 1858, including matrix multiplication and inverses. Every numerical calculation later in this book ultimately reduces to operations on matrices.
\end{didyouknow}
